more-experts-toy demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/more-experts-toy/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment
toy inspired by:

  Qiu, Acikalin, Lovelace, Belardi, Mulchandani, Gomes, Weinberger,
  "MoRE: Mixture of Reused Experts", Cornell University,
  arXiv:2609.18176 / COLM 2026
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.18176

Found via a bookmarked X post by @askalphaxiv:
  https://x.com/askalphaxiv/status/2116032693280571682

Official full-scale training code exists:
  https://github.com/EricQiu6/MoRE  (Apache-2.0)

That upstream stack targets DeepSeek-v3-style MoE pretraining on C4 at
114M–1.15B parameters and is unsuitable for this monorepo's CPU
clear-experiment standard. This app is therefore an **independent
clean-room toy** of the paper's core idea — shared expert pools across
adjacent layers (reuse factor R), per-layer routers, and learnable depth
embeddings — on a tiny character LM. No upstream source files are
vendored. Results do not claim to reproduce the paper's C4 / FineWeb /
downstream tables.

Corpus: a trimmed public-domain excerpt of Alice's Adventures in
Wonderland (Project Gutenberg) under data/tiny_corpus.txt.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Trained weights stay out of git (work/
is git-ignored).
